Interpretation
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Existential sector-vector realizability is trivial in the strong sense:
  every composition of n-1 into n sectors is realized by an explicit
  primitive speed set at an open time t=1/(nL).
Therefore HYP-2022's restriction is not global vector existence.
The real questions are fixed-clock menus, low-complexity realization,
observer anchoring, boundary compactification, and forced hitting of
the good face c_0=c_{n-1}=0 by every primitive clock.
The bounded forced intersections above are bad boundary fans, not LRC
witnesses: they come from times near 0 or 1 where almost all runners sit
next to the observer.  The good face is not a single forced vector.
